{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Additional reproduction from janitor approval on 2026-08-31. Multiple MCP comment_ticket mutations failed before writing after the full 181-second acquire budget. Holder samples crossed two compact-sweep processes: pid=49003 start=19655570 and later pid=86573 start=20943214, each reported pid_state=live and op=compact-sweep. The maintainer-requested retry failed with pid=86573 held=103s. This recurrence across PIDs means the incident is not explained solely by one permanent pid-49003 stamp; investigate repeated MCP-local sweeps, stale ownership metadata, and tracker-path/store-identity divergence. Immediately afterward, the local worktree CLI command rebar comment against literal-subaverage-dartfrog succeeded in 7.7s, proving the requested write itself and the local shared-store path were writable while the MCP path had repeatedly timed out. Read-only diagnostics used the worktree venv. rebar doctor --output json exited 1 with 14 mis-escalated-link findings, but every reported lock was free and lock_findings was empty: tickets-write-fcntl free, tickets-write-mkdir free, hlc free, enrich-drain free, compact-worker free, snapshot-gc-worker free. Doctor inspected /Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker; compare that exact path and inode/store identity with the MCP server path. rebar fsck --output json exited 1 with issue_count=27: 26 counted orphan_event findings plus one env_id_mismatch; it also reported ten status_fork_resolved observations as counted=false. The environment mismatch says current env b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126 has written under three other env IDs. These fsck findings are attached as store-health evidence, not asserted as the lock root cause. No doctor/fsck repair option and no force override was used. Please extend RCA to explain why MCP timed out while the local CLI immediately wrote and why doctor could not observe the recently blocking compact-sweep holder."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788236790390602001,"uuid":"0b64c8cb-9743-48d1-85bf-4f75b78ee012"}